The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ret = btrfs_next_leaf(root, path);
if (ret) 
    break;
```
Reason:
When `btrfs_next_leaf()` returns an error (negative value), the `replay_dir_deletes` function continues executing without properly handling the error and falls into a situation where the variable `@ret` can be incorrectly set to 0 after the `break;` statement, thereby misleading the caller into thinking the operation was successful.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (ret == 1)
    break;
else if (ret < 0)
    goto out;
```
Reason:
This patch introduces an additional conditional check that differentiates between a normal return value of 1 (indicating no more leaves to process) and a negative return value (indicating an error). On encountering an error, the code now jumps to the `out` label to handle the error appropriately, ensuring that the caller is informed of the issue instead of receiving a misleading success indicator.

